      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "Strix",
          "informationUri": "https://strix.ai",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CWE-407",
              "name": "CVE-2026-13149 in brace-expansion 1.1.15 / 2.1.1 (ReDoS-style exponential expansion DoS)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-13149 in brace-expansion 1.1.15 / 2.1.1 (ReDoS-style exponential expansion DoS)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The `brace-expansion` package resolved transitively into the repository's `pnpm-lock.yaml` at two vulnerable installations — `1.1.15` and `2.1.1` — is affected by **CVE-2026-13149**. The `expand()` function exhibits exponential-time complexity when processing a crafted string containing many consecutive non-expanding `{}` brace groups, allowing an attacker-controlled input to block the Node.js event loop."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The `brace-expansion` package resolved transitively into the repository's `pnpm-lock.yaml` at two vulnerable installations — `1.1.15` and `2.1.1` — is affected by **CVE-2026-13149**. The `expand()` function exhibits exponential-time complexity when processing a crafted string containing many consecutive non-expanding `{}` brace groups, allowing an attacker-controlled input to block the Node.js event loop.\n\nIf a code path in the build/CLI tooling (Metro bundler's `minimatch`/`glob` usage during Expo/React Native builds) ever passes attacker-influenced glob patterns to `brace-expansion.expand()`, an attacker could trigger CPU exhaustion and stall the bundler/build process (denial of service of the build pipeline). No confidentiality or integrity impact is associated with this CVE.\n\nBump the mobile workspace's `react-native` and `expo` dependencies to versions that resolve a patched `minimatch`/`glob`/`brace-expansion` chain, or force the resolution directly with a pnpm `pnpm.overrides` entry pinning `brace-expansion` to `>=1.1.16 <2.0.0 || >=2.1.2` in the root `package.json`. Re-run `pnpm install` and confirm the lockfile no longer resolves the vulnerable versions.",
                "markdown": "The `brace-expansion` package resolved transitively into the repository's `pnpm-lock.yaml` at two vulnerable installations — `1.1.15` and `2.1.1` — is affected by **CVE-2026-13149**. The `expand()` function exhibits exponential-time complexity when processing a crafted string containing many consecutive non-expanding `{}` brace groups, allowing an attacker-controlled input to block the Node.js event loop.\n\nIf a code path in the build/CLI tooling (Metro bundler's `minimatch`/`glob` usage during Expo/React Native builds) ever passes attacker-influenced glob patterns to `brace-expansion.expand()`, an attacker could trigger CPU exhaustion and stall the bundler/build process (denial of service of the build pipeline). No confidentiality or integrity impact is associated with this CVE.\n\nBump the mobile workspace's `react-native` and `expo` dependencies to versions that resolve a patched `minimatch`/`glob`/`brace-expansion` chain, or force the resolution directly with a pnpm `pnpm.overrides` entry pinning `brace-expansion` to `>=1.1.16 <2.0.0 || >=2.1.2` in the root `package.json`. Re-run `pnpm install` and confirm the lockfile no longer resolves the vulnerable versions."
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.3",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-407",
                  "CVE-2026-13149",
                  "stride:T",
                  "stride:I"
                ]
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/407.html"
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-400",
              "name": "CVE-2026-14257 in brace-expansion 1.1.15 / 2.1.1 (memory-exhaustion DoS)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-14257 in brace-expansion 1.1.15 / 2.1.1 (memory-exhaustion DoS)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The transitively-resolved `brace-expansion` installations (`1.1.15` and `2.1.1`) in the repository's `pnpm-lock.yaml` are affected by **CVE-2026-14257**. The `expand()` function bounds the result *count* via a `max` option but not the *length* of each result string, so chaining multiple brace groups lets an attacker keep the count under the limit while making each result progressively longer, causing memory exhaustion."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The transitively-resolved `brace-expansion` installations (`1.1.15` and `2.1.1`) in the repository's `pnpm-lock.yaml` are affected by **CVE-2026-14257**. The `expand()` function bounds the result *count* via a `max` option but not the *length* of each result string, so chaining multiple brace groups lets an attacker keep the count under the limit while making each result progressively longer, causing memory exhaustion.\n\nA crafted glob/brace pattern reaching `expand()` in the Metro/Expo CLI build toolchain could exhaust available memory and crash or hang the build process. No confidentiality or integrity impact is associated with this CVE.\n\nUpgrade `react-native`/`expo` to versions resolving a patched `minimatch`/`glob`/`brace-expansion` chain, or add a pnpm `pnpm.overrides` entry pinning `brace-expansion` to a fixed release (`1.1.17`, `2.1.3`, or later) in the root `package.json`, then regenerate the lockfile.",
                "markdown": "The transitively-resolved `brace-expansion` installations (`1.1.15` and `2.1.1`) in the repository's `pnpm-lock.yaml` are affected by **CVE-2026-14257**. The `expand()` function bounds the result *count* via a `max` option but not the *length* of each result string, so chaining multiple brace groups lets an attacker keep the count under the limit while making each result progressively longer, causing memory exhaustion.\n\nA crafted glob/brace pattern reaching `expand()` in the Metro/Expo CLI build toolchain could exhaust available memory and crash or hang the build process. No confidentiality or integrity impact is associated with this CVE.\n\nUpgrade `react-native`/`expo` to versions resolving a patched `minimatch`/`glob`/`brace-expansion` chain, or add a pnpm `pnpm.overrides` entry pinning `brace-expansion` to a fixed release (`1.1.17`, `2.1.3`, or later) in the root `package.json`, then regenerate the lockfile."
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-400",
                  "CVE-2026-14257",
                  "stride:D"
                ]
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/400.html"
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-835",
              "name": "CVE-2025-71329 in image-size 1.2.1 (infinite loop via zero-size box in JXL/HEIF parser)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-71329 in image-size 1.2.1 (infinite loop via zero-size box in JXL/HEIF parser)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The `image-size` package resolved to `1.2.1` in the repository's `pnpm-lock.yaml` is affected by **CVE-2025-71329**. Supplying a crafted image buffer with a zero-valued size field in a recognized box-type can trigger an infinite loop in the JXL or HEIF image parsers, permanently blocking the Node.js event loop."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The `image-size` package resolved to `1.2.1` in the repository's `pnpm-lock.yaml` is affected by **CVE-2025-71329**. Supplying a crafted image buffer with a zero-valued size field in a recognized box-type can trigger an infinite loop in the JXL or HEIF image parsers, permanently blocking the Node.js event loop.\n\nIf Metro (React Native's bundler) uses `image-size` to probe dimensions of an attacker-supplied image asset during a build or asset-serving step, a crafted JXL/HEIF file could hang the Node.js process indefinitely. No published fix is currently available; there is no confidentiality or integrity impact associated with this CVE.\n\nNo fixed version has been published upstream as of this scan. Track the `image-size` GitHub repository for a patched release and upgrade Metro/`react-native` once available. In the interim, avoid running Metro's dev server or bundler against untrusted image assets, and consider a pnpm `pnpm.overrides` pin once a fix ships.",
                "markdown": "The `image-size` package resolved to `1.2.1` in the repository's `pnpm-lock.yaml` is affected by **CVE-2025-71329**. Supplying a crafted image buffer with a zero-valued size field in a recognized box-type can trigger an infinite loop in the JXL or HEIF image parsers, permanently blocking the Node.js event loop.\n\nIf Metro (React Native's bundler) uses `image-size` to probe dimensions of an attacker-supplied image asset during a build or asset-serving step, a crafted JXL/HEIF file could hang the Node.js process indefinitely. No published fix is currently available; there is no confidentiality or integrity impact associated with this CVE.\n\nNo fixed version has been published upstream as of this scan. Track the `image-size` GitHub repository for a patched release and upgrade Metro/`react-native` once available. In the interim, avoid running Metro's dev server or bundler against untrusted image assets, and consider a pnpm `pnpm.overrides` pin once a fix ships."
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-835",
                  "CVE-2025-71329",
                  "stride:T",
                  "stride:I"
                ]
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/835.html"
            }
          ],
          "version": "1.5.3"
        }
